+++ b/docs/MPE3_Title_Pull.md
@@ -0,0 +1,94 @@
+# MPE3 title-only pull service
+
+This experimental service uses EasyFlash bank 58 and the stock 256-byte
+`EZFlashRAM` page. It does not activate the MPE2 virtual machine or initiate a
+C64 DMA operation. The C64 copies each published packet itself. Stock bank
+paging remains a separate cartridge feature; the dedicated title demo may omit
+erased bank 58 from its CRT chip table to avoid a paging request on selection.
+
+## Controls at $DFF0-$DFFF
+
+| Offset | Owner | Meaning |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| F0-F3 | C64 | Write `M3TP` before START. |
+| F4 | C64 | Write 1 to START with the staged root. |
+| F5 | Firmware | 0 idle, 1 loading, 2 running, 3 done, E0 error. |
+| F6 | C64 | ACK the last completely validated/applied packet sequence. |
+| F7 | Firmware | Sole packet commit sequence, written last after a barrier. |
+| F8-FA | C64 | Little-endian 24-bit asset offset in the raw EasyFlash image. |
+| FB | Firmware | Error code, or zero. |
+| FC | Firmware | Protocol version 1. |
+| FD | Firmware | Low byte of the zero-based current visit. |
+| FE | Firmware | Wrapping packet counter for diagnostics. |
+| FF | Firmware | Wrapping poll heartbeat; not a packet commit. |
+
+START latches only when the service is idle; repeating it while a packet is
+outstanding cannot replace that packet. A new START initializes ACK/commit to
+zero and sequence numbers then run 1..255,1..255. Leaving bank 58 abandons the
+service without writing another bank's mailbox. A new START is required to
+resume. A legacy accelerator owner makes START fail with error 1; it is never
+silently reset or upgraded by MPE3.
+Before a valid M3TP plus START, all bank-58 controls retain ordinary EasyFlash
+RAM read/write behavior. Firmware-owned control protection begins only after
+activation; the version control is initialized by START, not cartridge init.
+
+## Packet at $DF00-$DFEF
+
+Bytes 0-7 are `M3`, version 1, type, sequence, flags, payload length, and visit.
+A little-endian CRC16-CCITT follows the payload, covering the eight header bytes
+and payload with initial FFFF and polynomial 1021. The total copy length is
+`payload length + 10`, at most 238 bytes. Bytes beyond that length are undefined.
+
+- Type 1 CELL: 1..19 fixed twelve-byte records: u16 cell, eight bitmap bytes,
+  screen byte, color nibble. Cells are absolute target bytes, not XORs. Flag bit
+  0 marks base data; bit 1 marks its final packet. Base cells arrive in order
+  0..999. A reset-to-base visit resends this immutable base before its deltas.
+- Type 2 SID: exactly 26 payload bytes: three-bit retrigger mask, then the 25
+  register values for D400-D418. Clear the selected voice gates before applying
+  the snapshot. Flag bit 0 is a frame end, including unchanged SID snapshots.
+- Type 3 END: zero payload. ACK changes status to done. The final image remains.
+- Type 0E ERROR: one-byte error payload, matching FB. Status is E0.
+
+The producer never rewrites a pending packet until F6 equals F7. The consumer
+waits for a new nonzero F7, copies the exact packet, checks its embedded sequence
+and CRC (and rechecks F7), applies it, then ACKs. The C64 owns frame pacing:
+`holdTicks` SID/frame-end packets hold each visit. Music state is a candidate
+until that SID packet's ACK. Cell packet traffic never consumes a music tick.
+After all visits, SID frames continue over the final visual until all three
+score channels end, then END is published. This is a one-pass title sequence.
+
+## Asset and bounds
+
+`M3T1` is a 64-byte version-1 header: IDs at 6/7; u32 total at 8; u16 visit count
+at 12; nonzero default hold at 14; flags 7 at 15; five u32 offset/u32 length
+pairs at 16..55 for bitmap, screen, color, relative SID score, and visit stream.
+Body CRC32 is at 56; header CRC32 over bytes 0..59 is at 60. The sections are
+nonempty, contiguous, and consume the complete declared asset. Base lengths
+are exactly 8000/1000/1000, music is 24..8192 bytes, and the complete asset must
+fit the raw 1 MiB cartridge bounds.
+
+The existing room planes retain the captioned base. Music and visit bytes use
+a fixed 64 KiB RAM2 arena, so the 46,004-byte SQ1 title score + deltas require
+no optional PSRAM. Larger assets may use the existing EXTMEM VIEW arena when
+at least 2 MiB PSRAM is fitted; otherwise they fail closed. Shared cache
+metadata is invalidated before loading. Every byte is loaded through the
+bounded raw cartridge reader and CRC-checked before the first publication.
+
+Each visit is u16 cell count, u8 nonzero hold, u8 flags, then sorted twelve-byte
+target cells. Only reset-to-base flag 1 is accepted; the first visit must set
+it. Cells must be unique, strictly increasing, below 1000, and colors below 16.
+The declared visits must consume the delta section exactly.
+
+The score begins with three relative u24 channel offsets (first offset 9).
+Each channel is five-byte duration/frequency/amplitude records ending in FFFF
+duration. The native decoder preserves pulse width 0800, attack/decay 00,
+sustain from amplitude bits 0..3, pulse/noise selection from bit 4, and the
+existing noise-envelope retrigger/return-to-pulse behavior. Ended voices gate
+off. Score duration advances only when the C64 ACKs a SID frame.
+
+Errors: 1 legacy busy, 2 header/flags/header CRC, 3 bounds, 4 workspace unavailable,
+5 cartridge read, 6 body CRC, 7 cell/visit data, 8 score data.
+
+Run `node Source/Teensy/MinimalBoot/tests/mpe3-title-pull-conformance.mjs` for
+source-contract and executable wire/score model checks. A firmware build and
+physical TeensyROM+/C64 acceptance remain separate evidence.
